Client – Sends SQL queries to the database.

Database Engine – Processes queries and retrieves the required data.

Cache – Stores frequently accessed data in memory for faster retrieval.

Disk – Stores database information persistently.

Temp – Stores temporary tables and intermediate results.

Catalog – Stores metadata, such as table definitions and column information.

User Data – Contains actual database tables and records.

